# UI & typography consistency (player-facing)

This app is a **fixed mobile game UI** (390px design). Typography must look **identical across Android, iOS, and PWA** — not scaled by device settings or system fonts.

## Numeric text (required)

All **player-facing numbers** must use global classes from `app/globals.css`:

```tsx
<span className="numeric-text numeric-text--18" dir="ltr">
  {amount.toLocaleString("en-US")}
</span>
```

Available sizes: `--11`, `--12`, `--13`, `--14`, `--16`, `--17`, `--18`, `--20`, `--24`, `--25`, `--30`, `--32`, `--36`.

In CSS modules, prefer:

```css
.balanceAmount {
  composes: numeric-text numeric-text--18 from global;
}
```

### Applies to

Balances, coins, prices, countdowns, timers, room codes, draw numbers, player counts, leaderboard values, tournament stats, prize amounts, quantities, and any other **sensitive numeric UI**.

## Font rules for numbers

- **Use**: `Vazirmatn` (bundled via `app/layout.tsx`)
- **Required features**: `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums` and `font-feature-settings: "tnum" 1, "lnum" 1` (provided by `.numeric-text`)
- **Never use for numbers**: `Inter`, `Segoe UI`, `Arial`, `Roboto`, or other system UI fonts
- **Do not use** `.latin-number` for new code; it exists only for backward compatibility

## Forbidden for sensitive numeric UI

Do **not** use `rem`, `em`, `vw`, `vh`, or `clamp()` for font sizes on balances, coins, prices, countdowns, room codes, leaderboard values, or similar numeric labels.

Use **fixed `px`** via `numeric-text--{size}` or explicit `font-size: Npx` in module CSS that composes from `.numeric-text`.

## CSS module pattern

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.prizeValue {
  composes: numeric-text numeric-text--14 from global;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: #fcd34d;
}

/* ❌ BAD */
.prizeValue {
  font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 3.2vw, 1rem);
  font-family: "Inter", sans-serif;
}
```

## Out of scope (do not change unless asked)

Image-based buttons, menu card artwork, app shell width (`max-w-[390px]`), and layout structure.

## Before finishing any UI task

1. Search changed files for new numeric displays (`toLocaleString`, counts, timers, prices).
2. Confirm each uses `numeric-text numeric-text--{size}` (or composes from global).
3. Confirm no `rem`/`em`/`vw`/`clamp()` on sensitive numeric font sizes.
4. Confirm no system font fallbacks on number elements.
